@startuml
' AD-026; source ../use-cases/UC-026-duplicate-shared-outfit.md
' Draft v0.1, 2026-11-09; approved PR #4 / DD-007 scope, not implementation.
' Trace: FEAT-COM-002; BR-026; CAP-11; PBI-043; US-COM-003 AC.
' SRS: FR-COM-005, FR-COM-008; DATA-COM-001.
' Business Rules: BRULE-COM-001, BRULE-COM-002; BRULE-AUTH-001/007.
' Open policy: MVP-Q01, MVP-Q02, MVP-Q09; PRD Section 34.2. No provider / owner allocation selected.
title AD-026 - Duplicate shared inspiration as an independent outfit draft
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
|User|
start
:Deliberately start UC-026;
|CapsuleAI|
if (Source / affected-user access authorized?) then (Yes)
  :Identify intended source and user context;
else (Denied / unusable)
  :Explain access state; disclose no private data;
  :Offer renewed access or accessible source;
  stop
endif
|CapsuleAI|
:Identify accessible shared outfit
and permitted reusable representation;
:Attempt independent draft copy for requesting user;
if (Draft acceptance established?) then (Yes)
  :Show own editable outfit draft;
  |User|
  :Edit own draft;
  |CapsuleAI|
  :Keep creator original unchanged;
else (Failed / uncertain)
  :Explain actual outcome;
  :Offer source / draft outcome review before safe retry;
endif
note right
  A draft copy is not owned-garment ingestion.
  It grants no access to the creator private inventory.
  Source withdrawal / saved content policy remains open.
end note

stop
@enduml
